{"record_id":"entry-651","status":"pass","title":"EPA Denied a Petition to Revoke Chlorpyrifos Tolerances and Registrations in 2017","description_short":"In 2017, EPA denied PANNA and NRDC's petition to revoke chlorpyrifos tolerances and cancel its registrations.","description_medium":"In March 2017, EPA Administrator Scott Pruitt denied a petition from the Pesticide Action Network North America and the Natural Resources Defense Council. They sought to revoke chlorpyrifos food-residue tolerances and cancel its pesticide registrations. EPA said the science on possible neurodevelopmental effects remained unresolved and that review would continue. Later court and agency actions changed the tolerances’ status.","description_long":"On March 29, 2017, EPA Administrator Scott Pruitt signed an order denying a petition filed in 2007 by the Pesticide Action Network North America (PANNA) and the Natural Resources Defense Council (NRDC). The groups sought revocation of all chlorpyrifos food-residue tolerances and cancellation of the pesticide’s product registrations. EPA denied the remaining claims and continued the registration review.

EPA said that, despite years of study, the science on possible neurodevelopmental effects remained unresolved. It said more evaluation was needed before completing the human-health part of the review or taking associated action on tolerances. The 2017 order therefore denied the requested revocation and cancellation; it did not settle the later legal history or establish chlorpyrifos’s present status.

EPA issued a rule revoking all chlorpyrifos tolerances in August 2021. In November 2023, the Eighth Circuit vacated that rule and remanded the matter to EPA. The court’s mandate took effect on December 28, 2023, restoring the tolerances. The 2017 denial is one dated step in an ongoing regulatory history.","source_urls":["https://www.epa.gov/ingredients-used-pesticide-products/order-denying-petition-revoke-all-tolerances-pesticide","https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2017-03/documents/chlorpyrifos3b_order_denying_panna_and_nrdc27s_petitition_to_revoke_tolerances.pdf","https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2017-10/documents/session-5-chlorpyrifos-status-update.pdf","https://www.epa.gov/ingredients-used-pesticide-products/chlorpyrifos"],"source_fact_map":[{"url":"https://www.epa.gov/ingredients-used-pesticide-products/order-denying-petition-revoke-all-tolerances-pesticide","supported_facts":["In this Order, EPA denies a petition requesting that EPA revoke all tolerances for the pesticide chlorpyrifos under section 408(d) of the Federal Food, Drug, and Cosmetic Act and cancel all chlorpyrifos registrations under the Federal Insecticide, Fungicide and Rodenticide Act.","The petition was filed in September 2007 by the Pesticide Action Network North America (PANNA) and the Natural Resources Defense Council (NRDC)."]},{"url":"https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2017-03/documents/chlorpyrifos3b_order_denying_panna_and_nrdc27s_petitition_to_revoke_tolerances.pdf","supported_facts":["EPA has concluded that, despite several years of study, the science addressing neurodevelopmental effects remains unresolved and that further evaluation of the science during the remaining time for completion of registration review is warranted.","EPA is denying these Petition claims and intends to complete a full and appropriate review of the neurodevelopmental data before either finalizing the proposed rule or taking an alternative regulatory action.","In this document EPA denies a petition by PANNA and the NRDC to revoke pesticide tolerances and cancel pesticide registrations. This action may also be of interest to agricultural producers, food manufacturers, or pesticide manufacturers.","ACTION: Order."]},{"url":"https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2017-10/documents/session-5-chlorpyrifos-status-update.pdf","supported_facts":["On March 29, 2017, EPA issued an order denying a petition requesting that EPA revoke all tolerances for the pesticide chlorpyrifos under section 408(d) of the Federal Food, Drug, and Cosmetic Act and cancel all chlorpyrifos registrations under the Federal Insecticide, Fungicide and Rodenticide Act.","The petition was filed in September 2007 by the Pesticide Action Network North America and the Natural Resources Defense Council.","EPA intends to complete the registration review of chlorpyrifos by October 1, 2022."]},{"url":"https://www.epa.gov/ingredients-used-pesticide-products/chlorpyrifos","supported_facts":["In Aug. 2021, EPA released the Final Tolerance Rule for Chlorpyrifos, which revoked all tolerances for chlorpyrifos.","On Nov. 2, 2023, the U.S. Court of Appeals for the Eighth Circuit issued a ruling vacating EPA's final rule and remanding the matter to EPA for further proceedings.","As of the issuance of the Eighth Circuit's mandate on Dec. 28, 2023, all chlorpyrifos tolerances were automatically in effect once again."]}],"source_provenance":{"job":"web39-23","input":{"branch":"codex/web39-lightsprint-takeover-2026-10-05","commit":"23c3a4bc68a517c37a4bee60bef4b11490ef14fc","path":"data/neon-workbench/external/web39-lightsprint-takeover-2026-10-05/worker-23-input.jsonl","record_id":"entry-651"},"staged_record":{"path":"data/neon-workbench/external/continuous-finish-2026-10-04/descriptions-full-staged-finalization.jsonl","record_id":"entry-651","cloud_rescue_provenance":{"branch":"ls/3-trump-description-rescue-03-of-12-53-dis-CLUW","commit":"73eaadfda688f7dd75a5e3f86c80d4102dc55d7c","file":"data/neon-workbench/