{"record_id": "entry-5309", "status": "pass", "title": "Court Orders Trump to Pay $2 Million for Trump Foundation Misuse", "description_short": "A November 2019 court order required Trump to pay $2 million after misuse of Trump Foundation funds for his political interests.", "description_medium": "On November 7, 2019, New York Attorney General Letitia James announced a court order requiring Donald Trump to pay $2 million in damages for misuse of Trump Foundation assets during the 2016 campaign. Trump admitted misusing charitable funds. Settlements also imposed restrictions on future charitable service and directed the dissolved Foundation’s remaining assets to independent charities.", "description_long": "On November 7, 2019, New York Attorney General Letitia James announced that the New York Supreme Court had ordered Donald Trump to pay $2 million in damages for improperly using charitable assets to advance his political interests during the 2016 presidential primaries. The order formed part of the resolution of the state’s lawsuit against the Trump Foundation and its directors.

Trump admitted personally misusing Foundation funds. The admissions included allowing his campaign to control the timing, amounts and recipients of approximately $2.8 million raised through a January 2016 veterans fundraiser. He also admitted using charitable money to settle obligations of companies he controlled and purchasing a $10,000 portrait with Foundation funds.

The Foundation had agreed to dissolve under court supervision in December 2018. The resolution directed its remaining $1.78 million in assets and Trump’s damages payment to eight independent charities. It required training for the Trump children and imposed restrictions on Trump’s future charitable service, including independent oversight and a five-year reporting requirement if he formed a new charity.", "source_urls": ["https://ag.ny.gov/press-release/2019/ag-james-secures-court-order-against-donald-j-trump-trump-children-and-trump", "https://www.npr.org/2019/11/07/777287610/judge-says-trump-must-pay-2-million-over-misuse-of-foundation-funds", "https://talkingpointsmemo.com/muckraker/rewatching-trump-iowa-fundraiser-heart-attorney-general-lawsuit"], "source_fact_map": [{"url": "https://ag.ny.gov/press-release/2019/ag-james-secures-court-order-against-donald-j-trump-trump-children-and-trump", "reference": "turn6view0", "access_status": "readable", "supported_facts": ["November 7, 2019 AG announcement confirms $2 million damages order, admissions of Foundation misuse, court-supervised December 2018 dissolution, and future charitable-service restrictions.", "January 2016 fundraiser was campaign-controlled; Foundation grants approximately $2.8 million.", "Five-year requirement concerns reporting if Trump creates a new charity, not a five-year ban on heading charities."], "limitations": "Does not reconcile canonical January 28, 2016 date with original judgment/dissolution event."}, {"url": "https://www.npr.org/2019/11/07/777287610/judge-says-trump-must-pay-2-million-over-misuse-of-foundation-funds", "reference": "turn6view1", "access_status": "restricted URL", "supported_facts": [], "limitations": "No readable evidence."}, {"url": "https://talkingpointsmemo.com/muckraker/rewatching-trump-iowa-fundraiser-heart-attorney-general-lawsuit", "reference": "turn6view2", "access_status": "readable", "supported_facts": ["October 2018 TPM report recounts January 2016 fundraiser h